---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
import { TREC_TRACK_ACCEPTED, SHOW_PROJECTS } from '../config';

const toc = [
  { id: 'replacing-reviewers', label: 'Replacing human reviewers?' },
  { id: 'project-or-thesis', label: 'Project AI or thesis' },
  { id: 'medical-training', label: 'Medical training?' },
  { id: 'trec', label: 'Relationship to TREC' },
  { id: 'data-release', label: 'Data release' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Frequently asked questions" description="Answers to common questions about the workshop: human reviewers, medical training, TREC and data release." toc={toc}>
  <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>

  <section aria-labelledby="replacing-reviewers">
    <h2 id="replacing-reviewers">Is this replacing human reviewers?</h2>
    <p>
      No. The workshop measures what agents get right and wrong in a systematic review, and what that costs in
      human time and compute. Systems are compared under fixed human-effort budgets, including human screening
      followed by machine completion and model-routed selective review. The reference standard is a published
      review update, adjudicated by methodologists.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="project-or-thesis">
    <h2 id="project-or-thesis">Can I do this as my Project AI or my MSc thesis?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. The call is for MSc AI students at the University of Amsterdam, who can take the work as their
      Project AI or as their MSc thesis. The internship runs for at least eight weeks, the length of Project AI.
      Participants are appointed as interns and receive a light remuneration.
      {SHOW_PROJECTS && (
        <>
          Every project on the <a href={href('/projects')}>projects page</a> is sized for eight weeks and
          describes how it extends into a thesis. You do not choose a project when you apply.
        </>
      )}
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="medical-training">
    <h2 id="medical-training">Do I need medical training?</h2>
    <p>
      No. Search, stopping rules, extraction and evaluation are problems that an MSc AI prepares you for.
      Methodologists adjudicate the conclusions that each task is scored against.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="trec">
    <h2 id="trec">What is the relationship to TREC?</h2>
    <p>
      The workshop is designed to build the collection, baselines and validated metrics for {TREC_TRACK_ACCEPTED ? 'the' : 'a proposed'} TREC
      track on technology-assisted review and agentic evidence synthesis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="data-release">
    <h2 id="data-release">Will data be released?</h2>
    <p>
      Yes. The frozen literature collections, the review/update task pairs with adjudicated conclusions, the
      action-log format, baseline agents and the evaluation toolkit will all be released publicly.
      See <a href={href('/data-and-evaluation')}>data and evaluation</a> for how they fit together.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
  }
</style>
